comment.body:
Fixed the P2 type error: the registered visitor_invite tool returns `AgentToolResult<unknown>`, so the new test now runs `assert(Value.Check(visitorInviteDetailsSchema, invite.details))` before reading `invitationText`, following the existing visitor_list pattern in this file. Verified on the remote container: both test files pass (17 tests) and tsgo reports no visitor-access type errors.

On the remaining shipped-proof ask: the invitation path is exercised through the **registered tool with the real plugin registration and real execution path**, but I understand the external-PR gate wants a shipped Gateway entry point. visitor_access is a Gateway agent tool (no standalone CLI) and both changed bounds — inviter label and onboarding error — are human-facing strings that only a live Cloudflare Access deployment can feed with a boundary display name. A shipped Gateway would additionally need a real agent + model to invoke visitor_invite with operator authority. I'll leave that judgment to a maintainer; the discriminative red/green tests and the registered-tool output remain the committed evidence.

@clawsweeper re-review
